[[SECTION]]
MID: da6a98500c5ff8f6432b502636340827
UID: DOC-DEPLOYMENT-PUSH-DEPLOYMENT-database-and-schema-maintenance-boundary
TITLE: Database and schema maintenance boundary

[TEXT]
MID: bc85fbd6a55297aec75c8a01bc33749e
STATEMENT: >>>
After initial schema creation, image-only `deploy` supports only an unchanged migration fingerprint, API epoch, and persistence format. The owning migration change needs an independently reviewed and explicitly approved procedure that defines a pre-change encrypted backup, migration execution and verification, and a tested restore path. The [LINK: DOC-DEPLOYMENT-BACKUP-verify-a-candidate-ledger-on-a-restored-backup, isolated restore drill] can verify the candidate ledger against a restored backup copy. PostgreSQL roles and Podman secrets require separate recovery. Production activation remains subject to the compatibility gates and the existing protected first Backend activation or compatible update path.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
MID: 3b0900b7a2aee387c334b860825b0fdb
UID: DOC-DEPLOYMENT-PUSH-DEPLOYMENT-incompatible-release-refusal
TITLE: Incompatible release refusal

[TEXT]
MID: f813ae872843f383215352fef14504a9
STATEMENT: >>>
There is no coordinated pair or epoch-transition deployment path. Refuse an incompatible installed environment without modifying its writer, database or owner. A separately authorized clean install is available only after positively observing database absence; existing-data recovery remains a distinct operation.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
MID: d4e80a45441874504362f8c9a747fdbf
UID: DOC-DEPLOYMENT-PUSH-DEPLOYMENT-acceptance-order
TITLE: Acceptance order

[TEXT]
MID: 834e5efe08e1b516b986b0b5c0f6d233
STATEMENT: >>>
Run `bootstrap` and complete enrollment before requesting protected first activation. Enable automatic updates only for the installed API after ordinary backup and recovery acceptance. At that point the target has the `codexia` account, rootless Podman and user systemd, canonical database, management connector and publication gate, protected Podman secrets, the dedicated SSH key, and a pinned host key. The approved `auth-runtime` stage initializes an empty application schema during provisioning. The first `deploy` activation, with both explicit approvals, verifies its exact migration ledger. Later `deploy` runs apply compatible image updates. Keep the existing `sophia` storage outside this workflow.

Acceptance must record separate evidence for CI certification and VM behavior. On the target, verify dedicated Access Service Auth and pinned management SSH, first deployment from a clean `codexia` runtime with preserved or explicitly restored data, same-digest reapplication, a compatible update, a deliberately failing candidate and verified restoration, host-lock contention, service recovery after reboot, encrypted backup and isolated restore, and external application health through Cloudflare Tunnel.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
MID: 1649aafdc5a36ea4fc30e59fd659dd0f
UID: DOC-DEPLOYMENT-PUSH-DEPLOYMENT-backup-destination-policy
TITLE: Backup destination policy

[TEXT]
MID: a9488ee6b6d07acc8b20fc56efcbb818
STATEMENT: >>>
The operator provisions the [LINK: DOC-DEPLOYMENT-BACKUP-CONSOLE-OPERATIONS, VM backup runtime] with a private staging directory and the age recipient. The recipient's recovery identity stays in independent secret custody. An owner activates the destination in the ordinary Console. Complete the independent restore and operational acceptance before enabling automatic Backend updates.

For a compatible change to an installed API, Ansible acquires the host lock and checks the VM-local staging configuration. The executor pins the active Console revision and records the source and candidate identities before Ansible stops the writer. The same protected runner used by ordinary backup invokes `backup.sh` with the inherited lock descriptor. The executor verifies the ciphertext against the pinned off-VM policy. A successful deployment record carries the verified run ID.

Missing configuration or required preservation stops the update. A failed secondary destination permits activation only when the approved independent mount passes verification. When preservation fails after quiescing the writer, the transaction restores the prior API and publication state. Interrupted runs retain their recorded status for reconciliation.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
